hanged over  time  and now we're starting to apply overlap  of some of those  those those insights to the world of  data in  mlaps and data quality and pipelines and  transformations and other things  i think it's we're in a really golden  era of data tooling  and so um it's great to see um more  thoughtful people like yourself  you know applying um lessons learned in  in previous careers for previous  generations of their career and then  sort of bringing those best practices  and that mentality to the data  engineering the data science the  analytics world i think it's  it's definitely required and really  salute you for your clear thinking and  that  uh in that way thanks yeah it was great  to have you patrick um  thanks for for being with us and for  sharing your wisdom with our community  it's great being here  so just a couple announcements um before  we wrap  up i want to let people know that a data  council has been running our 2021  open source data tools survey it's  caught  on like wildfire in the community um  we've had  hundreds and hundreds of responses  thousands of tools  referenced in the survey there's one  more day to complete the survey  before friday tomorrow we'll put a link  to it in the chat window and so we'd  love it if  everyone listening would fill in your  favorite open source data tool share it  with your friends it's basically a one  survey question  we made it as dead simple and as  as quick to take as possible so you can  literally do it in 20 seconds so please  do that and sound off on your favorite  open source tools  in the community also just a reminder to  folks who are listening  i'm a four-time startup founder myself i  love to help engineers and other people  in our community figure out  how to get their companies off the  ground i have a few office hour slots  that i make available for the community  every month  i'd welcome you to um click through if  you want to talk to me for a half an  hour  share with your share with me your idea  get feedback  i love to have office hours with the  community and so um just wanted to put  the call out for folks there that might  want to take advantage of that  um finally next week we'll have matt  rocklin from  coiled the doubt the company behind desk  we're really excited about that
 

